{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/415642-dolphin-s-breath","id":415642,"title":"Dolphin's Breath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-22T14:16:38-08:00","id":415642,"title":"Dolphin's Breath","content":"Subsequent to my Water Breathing thread, I decided that the cleanest way to handle the problem was with a goblin contract. I present for evaluation <br /> <br /> DOLPHIN'S BREATH (\u2022)<br /> <br /> This Contract allows the invoker to hold her breath for truly amazing periods, even at high levels of activity, such as in combat. However, this contract is exhausting to use; upon its expiry, the changeling passes out. This is mechanically equivalent to taking bashing damage equal to the user's Health, with no roll allowed to remain conscious. This can push a character into lethal or aggravated injury. However, this damage is tracked separately, and heals at normal bashing rates and by normal bashing means.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Glamour<br /> Dice Pool: Stamina+Wyrd<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Catch: The character dives into salt water at least five metres deep.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The character can hold her breath for only one turn, even out of combat.<br /> <br /> Failure: Normal rules apply<br /> <br /> Success: The character can hold her breath for the full Stamina-based duration, even in combat<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Add Wyrd to the character's Stamina for purpose of determining duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:05:38-08:00","id":415740,"title":"","content":"Pretty cool. The catch could be harder to meet, though catch difficulty is always pretty variable.<br /> <br /> Pairing it with Eternal Spring 1 would work really well in overcoming the drawback, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T04:05:17-08:00","id":416348,"title":"","content":"Unconscious for 15 minutes and out of action for even longer unless there is somebody else who can cure you (and not even talking about the risk of dying)... who would ever use this contract for a few more minutes of breathing underwater? If there is nobody around to heal you, you are going to drown if you loose consciousness that long while in the water. It might be better to make it a set number of damage per turn/scene, that way you have at least some control over when to stop and an ability to heal yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T07:38:34-08:00","id":416489,"title":"","content":"Well, there's no risk of dying from the contract unless you're already badly injured or, as you say, can't get to somewhere you can breathe before the contract runs out. The latter is a very good reason to plan your dives carefully; the former is exactly the sort of thing that makes people regard goblin contracts as dubious goods at best. Also, I couldn't come up with a better idea for the drawback; any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T08:34:02-08:00","id":416509,"title":"","content":"Maybe, for the following scene, your speech is replaced with squeaks and pops? Like a dolphin? :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}